{"type":"system","subtype":"task_notification","task_id":"b89x90i3c","tool_use_id":"toolu_01RhCYwobqks9asoGz2Ziyrr","status":"completed","output_file":"/tmp/claude-441489/-scratch-users-kushinm-auto-psych-outer-loop-live-runs-run3-repo/12cf44ef-f4c4-4746-966c-a80d8d91b3c1/tasks/b89x90i3c.output","summary":"Background command \"D=/scratch/users/kushinm/auto-psych/outer_loop_live/run3/data/subjective_randomness/experiment2/model_loop/iter_2/candidate_5\nSRC=/scratch/users/kushinm/auto-psych/outer_loop_live/run3/data/subjective_randomness/experiment2/model_loop/models/person_side_habit_switch_belief.py\ncat << 'EOF' > $D/hypothesis.md\nRefinement of `person_side_habit_switch_belief`: people still judge a sequence random to the extent their own model of a fair coin (with a person-specific belief about how often chance switches) explains it better than the regular generators (a switch-biased Markov coin, a biased coin, and a repeating short motif with occasional slips), with the evidence weighed per flip, person-specific decisiveness and a person-specific side habit. The single change is in what people imagine a \"biased coin\" to be: they do not suspect heads-rigged and tails-rigged coins equally, but hold a lopsided prior (of fitted direction and strength) that trick coins are rigged towards heads, so a head-heavy sequence is more readily explained as coming from a rigged coin and looks less random than the mirror-image tail-heavy sequence — addressing the critique (surviving FDR) that people choose the sequence with more heads less often than an H/T-symmetric model allows.\nEOF\necho heads_rigged_coin_suspicion > $D/model_name.txt\npython3 - \"$SRC\" \"$D/candidate.py\" << 'PY'\nimport sys\ns=open(sys.argv[1]).read()\ndoc_old=s[:s.index('import math')]\ndoc='''\"\"\"Heads-rigged trick-coin suspicion in the per-person switch-belief chance-vs-motif judgment.\n\nRefinement of `person_side_habit_switch_belief`: a sequence looks random to the\nextent a fair coin (person-specific believed switch rate) explains it better\nthan the regular generators (Markov coin, biased coin, repeating motif with\nslips; unknowns integrated out), evidence weighed per flip by (n/5)**-gamma,\nperson-specific sensitivity and side habit. Single change: the biased-coin\ngenerator's prior over the heads rate is Beta(2*s, 2*(1-s)) with fitted\nasymmetry s (s = 0.5 recovers the uniform prior), so people suspect coins\nrigged towards heads (s > 0.5) more than towards tails; head-heavy sequences\nthen look less random than their tail-heavy mirror images.\n\"\"\"\n\n'''\ns=doc+s[len(doc_old):]\ns=s.replace('''    log_biased = _log_beta(h + 1, n - h + 1)\n    out = {\"k\": float(k), \"lm\": log_markov, \"lb\": log_biased}''','''    out = {\"k\": float(k), \"lm\": log_markov, \"h\": float(h)}''')\ns=s.replace('''        \"seq_lbias\": np.asarray([t[\"lb\"] for t in table], dtype=\"float64\"),''','''        \"seq_heads\": np.asarray([t[\"h\"] for t in table], dtype=\"float64\"),''')\ns=s.replace('''    seq_lbias = pm.Data(\"seq_lbias\", np.zeros(1, dtype=\"float64\"))''','''    seq_heads = pm.Data(\"seq_heads\", np.zeros(1, dtype=\"float64\"))''')\ns=s.replace('''    # Log marginal likelihood of each distinct sequence under the regular generators.''','''    # Asymmetric prior of the imagined trick coin: Beta(2s, 2(1-s)) over its\n    # heads rate (s > 0.5: coins rigged towards heads are suspected more).\n    logit_s = pm.Normal(\"logit_s\", mu=0.0, sigma=1.0)\n    s_heads = pm.Deterministic(\"s_heads\", pm.math.sigmoid(logit_s))\n    a_h = 2.0 * s_heads\n    a_t = 2.0 - a_h\n    seq_lbias = (\n        pt.gammaln(seq_heads + a_h) + pt.gammaln(seq_len - seq_heads + a_t)\n        - pt.gammaln(seq_len + 2.0)\n        - pt.gammaln(a_h) - pt.gammaln(a_t) + math.lgamma(2.0)\n    )\n\n    # Log marginal likelihood of each distinct sequence under the regular generators.''')\nopen(sys.argv[2],'w').write(s)\nPY\ngrep -n \"lbias\\|_log_beta\\|seq_heads\" $D/candidate.py\ncd /scratch/users/kushinm/auto-psych/outer_loop_live/runs/run3/repo && /scratch/users/kushinm/auto-psych/outer_loop_live/venv/bin/python -m src.pipelines.inner_loop.check_candidate --candidate-dir $D --responses /scratch/users/kushinm/auto-psych/outer_loop_live/run3/data/subjective_randomness/experiment2/model_loop/responses.csv 2>&1 | tail -5\" completed (exit code 0)","uuid":"4227ff64-d1c4-4108-94bd-39ab997c75fd","session_id":"12cf44ef-f4c4-4746-966c-a80d8d91b3c1"}
