{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfiiVUmgd97Tpr3nmuq51","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The candidate passed the self-check: it printed `OK`, with a finite ELPD-LOO of −2103.4 on the short smoke fit. That fit is not comparable to the incumbent's −2105.7, which came from a full fit.\n\n**Model:** `heads_rigged_coin_suspicion`, a refinement of `person_side_habit_switch_belief` (rank 1, statistically tied with the incumbent).\n\n**What changed:** only the imagined biased coin. The parent model averages its heads rate over a uniform prior, so it treats H and T the same. This version gives that heads rate a Beta(2s, 2(1−s)) prior with a fitted asymmetry `s`. When `s` is 0.5 it is the parent model again. When `s` is above 0.5, people suspect coins rigged towards heads more than coins rigged towards tails. A head-heavy sequence then looks less random than its tail-heavy mirror image.\n\n**Why:** it targets the critique finding that survives FDR, `heads_count_preference`. People chose the sequence with more heads 47.3% of the time, below the 48.8% the incumbent predicts, and no H/T-symmetric model can produce that. I left out the side-bias spread finding because the parent model already has a per-person side habit.\n\n**Caveats:**\n- **Possible near-duplicate:** the change adds one parameter on top of the parent, so the novelty gate may reject it if the asymmetry it fits is small.\n- **Convergence untested:** the self-check used one chain, so it could not check R-hat.\n- **Unreliable PSIS-LOO:** 7.5% of trials had Pareto k above 0.5 on the smoke fit, well over the 1% tolerance. That may hurt it at export, since the winner must have a reliable PSIS-LOO.\n\nFiles are in `…/experiment2/model_loop/iter_2/candidate_5/`:\n- `hypothesis.md`\n- `model_name.txt`\n- `candidate.py`"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2706,"cache_read_input_tokens":76190,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2706,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"12cf44ef-f4c4-4746-966c-a80d8d91b3c1","uuid":"d9a65580-70bf-441e-94ea-ebf64bde0455","timestamp":"2026-10-05T07:44:00.745Z","request_id":"req_011CfiiVUAU52u7oDP8PHSJn"}
